**What changed:** The Angular Service Worker `Driver` class (in `@angular/service-worker`, `packages/service-worker/worker/src/driver.ts`) now registers a `messageerror` event listener on the service worker scope, alongside the existing `fetch`, `message`, `push`, `notificationclick`, `notificationclose` and `pushsubscriptionchange` listeners: `this.scope.addEventListener('messageerror', (event) => this.onMessageError(event));` A new private `onMessageError(event: MessageEvent)` method logs deserialization failures through the existing `DebugHandler` (`this.debugger.log`) with the message "Message error occurred - data could not be deserialized" and context `Driver.onMessageError(origin: <event.origin>)`. This implements the Service Worker spec's `messageerror` event, which fires when a received message cannot be deserialized (corrupted data or unsupported formats), improving error detection and debugging (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/62834, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8255e0cf15353e9eee339ae01851e32c0e5e174d).

**Affects:** Applications using `@angular/service-worker` (`NgSWModule` / `ngswWorker`) whose service worker receives messages that fail deserialization; otherwise no application code is affected — this is internal driver behavior only.

**Action:** none — purely additive logging/handling inside the service worker driver; no code, config, or dependency changes required in upgrading applications.

**Before/after:**
