**Affects:** Applications registering an Angular Service Worker via `provideServiceWorker('ngsw-worker.js', {...})` (or `ServiceWorkerModule.register`) that want to author the service worker script as an ES module. Default behavior is unchanged.

**Action:** none; to opt in, add `type: 'module'` to the `SwRegistrationOptions` passed to `provideServiceWorker` and ensure the service worker script uses valid ES module syntax (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/62831, ).

