**What changed:** The `DataGroup` class in the Angular Service Worker (`@angular/service-worker`) now includes a private method `detectStorageFull()` that proactively checks storage capacity. This method uses the `navigator.storage.estimate()` API to calculate storage usage. If usage is at or exceeds 95% of the quota, it logs the message "Storage is full or nearly full" via `debugHandler.log()`. This method is invoked in `syncLru()` and `safeCacheResponse()` within `packages/service-worker/worker/src/data.ts`, replacing previous TODO comments with active monitoring. (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/62737, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/b65c3d5e195267dd90b2826d4615ced1328b1709)

**Affects:** Applications using `@angular/service-worker` with data groups (`DataGroup`) that may approach browser storage limits.

**Action:** none

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// packages/service-worker/worker/src/data.ts

// Before (20.1.x)
    } catch (err) {
      this.debugHandler.log(
        err as Error,
        `DataGroup(${this.config.name}@${this.config.version}).syncLru()`,
      );
      // TODO: Better detect/handle full storage; e.g. using
      // navigator.storage.
    }

// After (20.2.x)
    } catch (err) {
      this.debugHandler.log(
        err as Error,
        `DataGroup(${this.config.name}@${this.config.version}).syncLru()`,
      );
      await this.detectStorageFull();
    }
  }

  private async detectStorageFull() {
    try {
      const estimate = await navigator.storage.estimate();
      const {quota, usage} = estimate;

      if (typeof quota !== 'number' || typeof usage !== 'number') {
        return;
      }

      const usagePercentage = (usage / quota) * 100;
      const isStorageFull = usagePercentage >= 95;

      if (isStorageFull) {
        this.debugHandler.log(
          'Storage is full or nearly full',
          `DataGroup(${this.config.name}@${this.config.version}).detectStorageFull()`,
        );
      }
    } catch {
      // Error estimating storage, possibly by unsupported browser.
    }
  }
```

**What changed:** The Angular Service Worker `Driver` class (`packages/service-worker/worker/src/driver.ts`) now registers an `unhandledrejection` event listener on the service worker scope: `this.scope.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => this.onUnhandledRejection(event));`. A new private method `onUnhandledRejection(event: PromiseRejectionEvent)` logs the failure via the `DebugHandler` debugger: `this.debugger.log('Unhandled promise rejection occurred', `Driver.onUnhandledRejection(reason: ${event.reason})`)`. This makes previously silent promise rejections inside the service worker visible in the Angular DevTools / `ngsw` debug log, instead of failing silently (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/63059, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/3b214d20403160ab73e65dca0352545efd577c31). The test harness `SwTestHarnessImpl` (`packages/service-worker/worker/testing/scope.ts`) also gained a `handleUnhandledRejection(reason: any)` helper for tests.

**Affects:** Applications using `@angular/service-worker` (`ngsw`); no application code changes — only additional debug log entries appear when unhandled rejections occur in the service worker.

**Action:** none. Optionally re-verify service worker debug logs (via the `/ngsw/` debug inspection or `DebugHandler` logs) to observe the new "Unhandled promise rejection occurred" entries.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// After (packages/service-worker/worker/src/driver.ts)
this.scope.addEventListener('messageerror', (event) => this.onMessageError(event));
this.scope.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => this.onUnhandledRejection(event));

private onUnhandledRejection(event: PromiseRejectionEvent): void {
  // Handle unhandled promise rejections in the service worker.
  // This is for debugging and preventing silent failures.
  this.debugger.log(
    `Unhandled promise rejection occurred`,
    `Driver.onUnhandledRejection(reason: ${event.reason})`,
  );
}
```

